1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,130
You woke up already tired of a day that has not even happened yet.

2
00:00:04,130 --> 00:00:14,180
You are lying there in the dark, before the alarm, looking at the ceiling, and your mind has already run ahead of you into hours you have not lived yet.

3
00:00:14,180 --> 00:00:19,920
There is a conversation waiting for you today, and you do not know how it is going to go.

4
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:24,840
There is news you are waiting on, and you have no say in when it arrives.

5
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:31,560
There is a person you will have to face, and you have already rehearsed it twice before your feet touched the floor.

6
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:37,310
And the work you did not finish yesterday is still sitting there, leaning against this morning.

7
00:00:37,310 --> 00:00:39,020
I know that feeling.

8
00:00:39,020 --> 00:00:48,600
I have prayed on mornings like this one, with my eyes still closed and my chest already tight, asking God for strength I could not find on my own.

9
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:54,820
So before you get up, before this day starts asking things of you, stay here with me for a moment.

10
00:00:54,820 --> 00:00:58,560
Because here is what I want you to hear before we pray.

11
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:03,220
Today is not an empty room that you are the first one to walk into.

12
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:06,970
It is a road, and there are already footprints on it.

13
00:01:06,970 --> 00:01:09,960
You are not the one opening this day.

14
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:12,070
You are not the scout.

15
00:01:12,070 --> 00:01:18,750
You are not the one who has to see around every corner and prepare for every version of what might happen.

16
00:01:18,750 --> 00:01:23,090
Someone stood at the end of this day long before you stood at the beginning of it.

17
00:01:23,090 --> 00:01:26,190
He has already been in the room you are dreading.

18
00:01:26,190 --> 00:01:29,510
He has already heard the words that have not been said to you yet.

19
00:01:29,510 --> 00:01:32,290
He knows what the phone call will say.

20
00:01:32,290 --> 00:01:37,440
He knows which of the things you are worrying about right now will never happen at all.

21
00:01:37,440 --> 00:01:41,350
And he did not wake up this morning trying to catch up with your life.

22
00:01:41,350 --> 00:01:44,720
You do not have to carry the whole day at once.

23
00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:50,340
You only have to walk it, one hour at a time, behind someone who has already been there.

24
00:01:50,340 --> 00:01:55,300
There is a promise in Deuteronomy, chapter thirty-one, verse eight.

25
00:01:55,300 --> 00:02:05,780
Moses was old, and he was handing an entire nation over to a younger man named Joshua, and Joshua was about to walk into a land he had never set foot in.

26
00:02:05,780 --> 00:02:15,740
And Moses told him that God himself would go ahead of him, that God would be with him, and that God would not fail him and would not abandon him.

27
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:17,730
He goes before you.

28
00:02:17,730 --> 00:02:19,340
He stays with you.

29
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:21,070
He does not leave.

30
00:02:21,070 --> 00:02:23,730
And I want you to notice something about that.

31
00:02:23,730 --> 00:02:27,110
God did not say those words to a man on an easy road.

32
00:02:27,110 --> 00:02:31,360
Right after that promise, Joshua walked into years of war.

33
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:35,220
So this is not a prayer that pretends today will be simple.

34
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:46,090
This is a prayer for the guarding you will never see, for your name to be spoken kindly in rooms you are not standing in, and for the thing sitting in your road to be moved before you reach it.

35
00:02:46,090 --> 00:02:52,530
But there is a harder question inside that verse, and we are going to bring it to God before we finish.

36
00:02:52,530 --> 00:02:55,070
So loosen your grip on this day.

37
00:02:55,070 --> 00:02:57,060
Turn your face toward him.

38
00:02:57,060 --> 00:03:02,240
I am going to start speaking to him now, and you can pray these words with me.

39
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:10,190
Father, before I ask you for a single thing about today, let me thank you for something I slept straight through.

40
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:13,820
For about seven hours I was not guarding anything.

41
00:03:13,820 --> 00:03:15,610
I was not praying.

42
00:03:15,610 --> 00:03:17,600
I was not deciding.

43
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:19,910
I was not even aware that I existed.

44
00:03:19,910 --> 00:03:25,180
And the world kept turning, and this house kept standing, and I woke up.

45
00:03:25,180 --> 00:03:28,430
And it is not only last night that I want to thank you for.

46
00:03:28,430 --> 00:03:32,030
It is all the days you went ahead of me that I never found out about.

47
00:03:32,030 --> 00:03:35,320
There was a conversation I still call a coincidence.

48
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:44,350
Someone said the right sentence to me at the right hour, and it changed the direction I was walking, and I thanked the person and never thanked you.

49
00:03:44,350 --> 00:03:47,580
There is a road I have driven a thousand times.

50
00:03:47,580 --> 00:03:51,300
A thousand times, and nothing has ever happened on it.

51
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:54,250
I have never counted that as an answered prayer.

52
00:03:54,250 --> 00:03:56,600
And there were words I almost said.

53
00:03:56,600 --> 00:03:58,750
I had them in my mouth.

54
00:03:58,750 --> 00:04:04,118
Something in me went quiet instead, and I do not know what it would have cost me if I had spoken them.

55
00:04:04,118 --> 00:04:06,138
So this is what I am learning.

56
00:04:06,138 --> 00:04:11,048
You were already going before me on days I did not even think to ask you to.

57
00:04:11,048 --> 00:04:15,228
Your kindness was working in hours I have no memory of at all.

58
00:04:15,228 --> 00:04:17,888
You never asked me to notice.

59
00:04:17,888 --> 00:04:21,098
Thank you for the mercy I slept straight through.

60
00:04:21,098 --> 00:04:24,188
You have never arrived somewhere after I did.

61
00:04:24,188 --> 00:04:26,088
That is who you are.

62
00:04:26,088 --> 00:04:29,158
Before the meeting, you were in the room.

63
00:04:29,158 --> 00:04:32,348
Before the phone rang, you knew the voice.

64
00:04:32,348 --> 00:04:40,458
Before I was born into this family, you had already chosen the century and the country and the people I would open my eyes on.

65
00:04:40,458 --> 00:04:51,848
I have watched someone go into a room ahead of a child, checking whether the floor was clear and the window was shut, so the child could walk in and simply be a child.

66
00:04:51,848 --> 00:04:56,678
That is the smallest picture I have of you, and it is still too small.

67
00:04:56,678 --> 00:05:00,158
You are not waiting to see how today turns out.

68
00:05:00,158 --> 00:05:02,938
Nothing about it is information to you.

69
00:05:02,938 --> 00:05:06,048
Nothing about it caught you off guard while I slept.

70
00:05:06,048 --> 00:05:09,438
You have never had to be told what a day would hold.

71
00:05:09,438 --> 00:05:12,978
Nations have risen and fallen inside your patience.

72
00:05:12,978 --> 00:05:17,438
And you still know what my name sounds like when I say it to myself.

73
00:05:17,438 --> 00:05:21,398
You were already God before there was a morning to wake up into.

74
00:05:21,398 --> 00:05:23,438
There was no first day for you.

75
00:05:23,438 --> 00:05:31,438
When the first light was made, you were the one who spoke it, and you already knew this hour, and this room, and the person breathing in it.

76
00:05:31,438 --> 00:05:37,698
I am praying to a God who was never young, and who has never needed rest to be ready for me.

77
00:05:37,698 --> 00:05:40,788
I am not asking you for anything in this moment.

78
00:05:40,788 --> 00:05:45,598
I only want to say it plainly, out loud, at the start of the day.

79
00:05:45,598 --> 00:05:48,488
You are never the one arriving late.

80
00:05:48,488 --> 00:05:52,998
I already made a plan for today, and I made it without asking you.

81
00:05:52,998 --> 00:05:55,948
I did it before my eyes were fully open.

82
00:05:55,948 --> 00:06:01,938
There is a list in my head that I wrote by myself, and I did not bring you one line of it.

83
00:06:01,938 --> 00:06:04,858
I decided what mattered.

84
00:06:04,858 --> 00:06:06,738
I decided the order.

85
00:06:06,738 --> 00:06:11,098
I decided who deserved my patience and who did not.

86
00:06:11,098 --> 00:06:13,888
And then I called it being responsible.

87
00:06:13,888 --> 00:06:17,348
Self reliance is the quietest way I disobey you.

88
00:06:17,348 --> 00:06:19,958
It never feels like rebellion.

89
00:06:19,958 --> 00:06:22,368
It feels like being capable.

90
00:06:22,368 --> 00:06:25,108
It feels like maturity.

91
00:06:25,108 --> 00:06:30,278
But it is still me walking out in front of the God who said he would go first.

92
00:06:30,278 --> 00:06:32,608
And I do it because I am afraid.

93
00:06:32,608 --> 00:06:37,008
If I hold the plan, I can pretend I am holding the outcome.

94
00:06:37,008 --> 00:06:38,848
Forgive me for that.

95
00:06:38,848 --> 00:06:46,698
Not with shame that keeps me talking about myself, but with mercy that turns me around and points me back at you.

96
00:06:46,698 --> 00:06:49,068
And you did not need me to explain it.

97
00:06:49,068 --> 00:06:56,348
You have watched me do this for years, and you have never once stopped going ahead of me while I insisted on going first.

98
00:06:56,348 --> 00:06:59,658
Nothing I confessed this morning surprised you.

99
00:06:59,658 --> 00:07:03,448
So let me read it to you, line by line, since I never did.

100
00:07:03,448 --> 00:07:05,008
Line one.

101
00:07:05,008 --> 00:07:07,018
The thing I am dreading.

102
00:07:07,018 --> 00:07:08,458
Line two.

103
00:07:08,458 --> 00:07:10,718
The thing I keep postponing.

104
00:07:10,718 --> 00:07:12,248
Line three.

105
00:07:12,248 --> 00:07:15,028
The person I do not know how to answer.

106
00:07:15,028 --> 00:07:18,598
Line four is the email I have not opened.

107
00:07:18,598 --> 00:07:25,418
It has been sitting there since last night, and I have looked at the sender's name four times without touching it.

108
00:07:25,418 --> 00:07:31,188
Line five is the part of today that has no line, because I cannot see it yet.

109
00:07:31,188 --> 00:07:33,938
So take the order away from me.

110
00:07:33,938 --> 00:07:36,078
You have never needed my sequence.

111
00:07:36,078 --> 00:07:38,338
Put the hard thing where you want it.

112
00:07:38,338 --> 00:07:47,928
Give me the strength for it at the hour it comes, not now, at dawn, when I am trying to feel strong about something that is still nine hours away.

113
00:07:47,928 --> 00:07:52,298
It is on the table now, and I am not the one deciding the order.

114
00:07:52,298 --> 00:07:58,858
And Father, as I hand you this day, there are three things I need from you that I cannot do for myself.

115
00:07:58,858 --> 00:08:11,368
There is a way people walk the edges of a property before the sun is up, checking gates that no one else thinks about, testing a latch twice, looking at the ground for anything that should not be there.

116
00:08:11,368 --> 00:08:14,028
Do that with this day, Father.

117
00:08:14,028 --> 00:08:19,408
Go around the edges of it before I get there, and stand at the hours I cannot see.

118
00:08:19,408 --> 00:08:24,028
And there is one place I need you to guard that I do not like admitting.

119
00:08:24,028 --> 00:08:26,128
Guard me from myself.

120
00:08:26,128 --> 00:08:31,548
Because most of what could go wrong today will not come at me from outside.

121
00:08:31,548 --> 00:08:33,518
It will come out of me.

122
00:08:33,518 --> 00:08:42,818
The third time someone interrupts my work with something they could have handled alone, there is a sentence already loaded in my chest, and it is not a kind one.

123
00:08:42,818 --> 00:08:45,158
Guard my mouth in that second.

124
00:08:45,158 --> 00:08:50,428
Guard the message I would type in four seconds and regret for four weeks.

125
00:08:50,428 --> 00:08:54,998
Guard the decision I would make quickly just to make the discomfort stop.

126
00:08:54,998 --> 00:08:58,638
Guard the tone I use with the people who have to live with me.

127
00:08:58,638 --> 00:09:04,208
They did not cause the pressure I am carrying, and they should not be the ones who pay for it.

128
00:09:04,208 --> 00:09:13,398
Guard my body on the road today, and the people I love while they are far from me, and the ones under my roof who cannot protect themselves.

129
00:09:13,398 --> 00:09:18,988
And if there are children who carry my name, guard them where I cannot see them.

130
00:09:18,988 --> 00:09:24,478
I know that being your child has never meant that nothing hard ever reaches me.

131
00:09:24,478 --> 00:09:29,238
I have read too much of your word to promise myself a day with no trouble in it.

132
00:09:29,238 --> 00:09:34,128
Joshua had this promise and still crossed a river into a fight.

133
00:09:34,128 --> 00:09:36,768
So I am not asking for a padded life.

134
00:09:36,768 --> 00:09:38,978
I am asking for a guarded one.

135
00:09:38,978 --> 00:09:45,358
And if something hard does reach me today, do not let it reach me while I am standing there alone.

136
00:09:45,358 --> 00:09:48,588
Walk the edges of this day before I do.

137
00:09:48,588 --> 00:09:52,378
Father, what happens in the rooms I am not standing in?

138
00:09:52,378 --> 00:09:57,208
Because decisions get made about my life in places I will never be invited into.

139
00:09:57,208 --> 00:10:01,308
A short conversation between two people who barely know me.

140
00:10:01,308 --> 00:10:05,518
A list on someone's desk with my name on the seventh line.

141
00:10:05,518 --> 00:10:10,018
A meeting today where my work is discussed and I am not there to explain it.

142
00:10:10,018 --> 00:10:15,538
Your word says that you surround the righteous with favor like a shield.

143
00:10:15,538 --> 00:10:17,908
Here is one way I have come to picture it.

144
00:10:17,908 --> 00:10:22,328
Favor is your name spoken kindly in a room you are not standing in.

145
00:10:22,328 --> 00:10:25,628
And I am not righteous because of anything I achieved.

146
00:10:25,628 --> 00:10:28,088
I have nothing to bring to that word.

147
00:10:28,088 --> 00:10:33,768
I am righteous because of what Christ did, and that is the only reason I can ask this at all.

148
00:10:33,768 --> 00:10:35,888
So speak for me today.

149
00:10:35,888 --> 00:10:40,348
Where I am misunderstood, let someone remember the truth about me.

150
00:10:40,348 --> 00:10:44,328
Where my work is being weighed, let it be weighed fairly.

151
00:10:44,328 --> 00:10:49,198
Where someone has already decided who I am, soften them enough to look again.

152
00:10:49,198 --> 00:10:52,438
Give me the kind of favor I cannot manufacture.

153
00:10:52,438 --> 00:10:54,288
I can prepare.

154
00:10:54,288 --> 00:10:56,208
I can be honest.

155
00:10:56,208 --> 00:10:58,048
I can do good work.

156
00:10:58,048 --> 00:11:03,668
But I cannot make a stranger trust me, and I cannot follow my own name into a room and defend it.

157
00:11:03,668 --> 00:11:09,268
Let the person who holds the answer be kinder toward me than anything I have done deserves.

158
00:11:09,268 --> 00:11:11,468
Not because I earned it.

159
00:11:11,468 --> 00:11:13,748
Because you went in first.

160
00:11:13,748 --> 00:11:18,418
And if the answer in that room is no, let me find out that you were still in it.

161
00:11:18,418 --> 00:11:24,238
Let me be able to look back in a year and see that the no was one of the ways you went ahead of me.

162
00:11:24,238 --> 00:11:30,858
I have had answers I begged for that would have cost me everything, and I only understood that later.

163
00:11:30,858 --> 00:11:34,158
Speak my name in the rooms I cannot enter.

164
00:11:34,158 --> 00:11:43,238
Something heavy has been sitting in my road for a long time now, the way a fallen tree lies across a lane and every car has to turn around.

165
00:11:43,238 --> 00:11:45,688
I know exactly what mine is.

166
00:11:45,688 --> 00:11:48,478
I do not need a moment to think about it.

167
00:11:48,478 --> 00:11:50,508
There is the debt I am carrying.

168
00:11:50,508 --> 00:12:02,628
I have made peace with the number and I have not made peace with what it does to me, the way it stands behind every ordinary decision, the way it turns a small purchase into an argument in my own head.

169
00:12:02,628 --> 00:12:06,718
There is the file I sent in eight months ago that nobody has answered.

170
00:12:06,718 --> 00:12:10,528
Not a refusal, which I could grieve and move on from.

171
00:12:10,528 --> 00:12:11,990
Silence.

172
00:12:11,990 --> 00:12:15,380
A form sitting in a building I have never seen.

173
00:12:15,380 --> 00:12:18,810
And there is the fortieth application.

174
00:12:18,810 --> 00:12:20,860
I remember the first one.

175
00:12:20,860 --> 00:12:27,400
I remember how carefully I wrote it, and how much of me went into it, and how little of me is left in the fortieth.

176
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:30,330
You are the God who moves what will not move.

177
00:12:30,330 --> 00:12:32,420
You did it to a sea.

178
00:12:32,420 --> 00:12:35,450
You did it to a stone at the mouth of a grave.

179
00:12:35,450 --> 00:12:42,020
Nothing in my road is heavier than what you have already moved, and I am not going to pretend I have earned that.

180
00:12:42,020 --> 00:12:45,520
And you have already been standing where that thing is sitting.

181
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:49,760
You did not arrive there this morning when I finally told you about it.

182
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:52,140
You were there before it fell.

183
00:12:52,140 --> 00:12:53,730
So move it.

184
00:12:53,730 --> 00:12:57,280
And if you will not move it today, then move me.

185
00:12:57,280 --> 00:13:03,230
Give me another road, or give me the strength to stand in front of this one without falling apart.

186
00:13:03,230 --> 00:13:08,330
Change my situation, or change what my situation is able to do to me.

187
00:13:08,330 --> 00:13:17,360
But do not leave me here believing that this is the end of my story, because you have never written a story that way, and you are not starting today.

188
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:22,440
Move it, or move me, but do not leave me standing here.

189
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:25,460
You went ahead of me into yesterday too.

190
00:13:25,460 --> 00:13:28,190
And yesterday was still hard.

191
00:13:28,190 --> 00:13:32,630
I prayed almost these same words at almost this same hour.

192
00:13:32,630 --> 00:13:34,110
I meant them.

193
00:13:34,110 --> 00:13:40,340
And then the day came, and it was heavy, and I ended it more tired than I started it.

194
00:13:40,340 --> 00:13:44,400
So I want to say the honest thing instead of the polite thing.

195
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:48,960
Sometimes I do not understand what your going before me actually does.

196
00:13:48,960 --> 00:13:50,790
I believe you were there.

197
00:13:50,790 --> 00:13:53,270
I just could not feel the difference.

198
00:13:53,270 --> 00:13:59,640
And yet when I look back at yesterday honestly, there are two places where it could have gone worse and did not.

199
00:13:59,640 --> 00:14:02,450
I did not notice either one at the time.

200
00:14:02,450 --> 00:14:06,070
I was measuring the whole day by how heavy it felt.

201
00:14:06,070 --> 00:14:12,120
Maybe you were there in exactly the way you promised, and I was reading the wrong evidence.

202
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:15,490
And then I remember who first received this promise.

203
00:14:15,490 --> 00:14:21,650
Moses said it to Joshua, and what Joshua walked into next was not comfort.

204
00:14:21,650 --> 00:14:24,120
It was years of war.

205
00:14:24,120 --> 00:14:26,490
Campaign after campaign.

206
00:14:26,490 --> 00:14:28,040
Losses.

207
00:14:28,040 --> 00:14:31,100
A whole generation of hard mornings.

208
00:14:31,100 --> 00:14:34,400
The promise was never that the road would be easy.

209
00:14:34,400 --> 00:14:39,960
The promise was that Joshua would not walk it first, and would not walk it alone.

210
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:49,090
In Habakkuk, chapter two, verse three, the prophet is told that what God has spoken has an appointed time, and that it will not lie.

211
00:14:49,090 --> 00:14:52,660
I am not going to use that verse to tell you what you owe me.

212
00:14:52,660 --> 00:14:55,520
I am going to use it to say something about you.

213
00:14:55,520 --> 00:15:00,200
You keep appointments I cannot see on a calendar nobody has shown me.

214
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:06,310
You are never disorganized, and never too busy with the size of the world to keep a date you set for me.

215
00:15:06,310 --> 00:15:12,390
You are deliberate, and you are kind, and those two things have never been in conflict in you.

216
00:15:12,390 --> 00:15:16,590
Habakkuk went up on the watchtower to wait and to keep looking.

217
00:15:16,590 --> 00:15:19,440
He did not stop asking hard questions.

218
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:22,100
He simply asked them from a higher place.

219
00:15:22,100 --> 00:15:24,640
So put me on that tower this morning.

220
00:15:24,640 --> 00:15:27,650
Let me wait without becoming bitter.

221
00:15:27,650 --> 00:15:29,910
Let me ask without accusing you.

222
00:15:29,910 --> 00:15:33,420
Let me keep watching for you in the hours ahead.

223
00:15:33,420 --> 00:15:36,430
You have not forgotten what I asked you for.

224
00:15:36,430 --> 00:15:42,490
Right now, while I am sitting here, someone is already in the hardest part of their day.

225
00:15:42,490 --> 00:15:46,990
Somewhere a person is driving to an appointment they have not told anyone about.

226
00:15:46,990 --> 00:15:51,660
They will hear a result today, and they made that drive alone on purpose.

227
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:53,970
Go before them into that room.

228
00:15:53,970 --> 00:15:56,860
Guide the doctors and nurses who care for them.

229
00:15:56,860 --> 00:15:59,110
Bless the medicine and the treatments.

230
00:15:59,110 --> 00:16:04,860
Someone is putting on new clothes for the first day of a job, and they are not sure they can do it.

231
00:16:04,860 --> 00:16:06,660
Steady their hands.

232
00:16:06,660 --> 00:16:12,290
A shop owner is opening the ledger, and the numbers are the same numbers they were last week.

233
00:16:12,290 --> 00:16:16,520
Give them one good idea and one unexpected customer.

234
00:16:16,520 --> 00:16:21,260
Someone will have to say a hard sentence to a person they love before tonight.

235
00:16:21,260 --> 00:16:25,340
Give them words that heal instead of words that win.

236
00:16:25,340 --> 00:16:29,880
And someone finally fell asleep an hour ago after being awake all night.

237
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:32,810
Let them rest a little longer than they planned.

238
00:16:32,810 --> 00:16:40,190
You are going ahead of every one of them, by name, at the same time, without ever dividing your attention.

239
00:16:40,190 --> 00:16:43,920
Go before every window that lit up this morning.

240
00:16:43,920 --> 00:16:47,340
And now the ones nobody is praying for.

241
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:52,990
There is a person who lives alone, and today not one voice will say their name out loud.

242
00:16:52,990 --> 00:16:54,610
Not at a table.

243
00:16:54,610 --> 00:16:56,270
Not on a phone.

244
00:16:56,270 --> 00:17:00,700
They will speak to a cashier and that will be the conversation of their day.

245
00:17:00,700 --> 00:17:03,040
Say their name, Father.

246
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:08,120
Let them be certain, somehow, that they were thought of before the sun came up.

247
00:17:08,120 --> 00:17:13,220
There is a person who left church because church is where they were hurt.

248
00:17:13,220 --> 00:17:15,000
They still love you.

249
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:21,030
They just cannot walk back through that door yet, and they have stopped telling anyone that they pray.

250
00:17:21,030 --> 00:17:22,710
Go before them.

251
00:17:22,710 --> 00:17:24,800
Do not send them a lecture.

252
00:17:24,800 --> 00:17:26,750
Send them someone safe.

253
00:17:26,750 --> 00:17:30,900
Remind them that you never left when the people did.

254
00:17:30,900 --> 00:17:39,750
There is a person waking up in a country that is not the country they were born in, several time zones away from everyone who remembers them as a child.

255
00:17:39,750 --> 00:17:45,570
They will work today in a second language, and be brave all day, and be homesick at night.

256
00:17:45,570 --> 00:17:48,860
Go ahead of them into their loneliness.

257
00:17:48,860 --> 00:17:53,780
And there is a person who will be treated unfairly at work before this day is over.

258
00:17:53,780 --> 00:18:00,190
They will be spoken to in a way no one should be spoken to, and they will need the job too much to answer back.

259
00:18:00,190 --> 00:18:02,090
Stand beside them.

260
00:18:02,090 --> 00:18:05,400
Guard their dignity when they cannot defend it.

261
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:08,280
You know each of them the way you know me.

262
00:18:08,280 --> 00:18:10,210
Not as a category.

263
00:18:10,210 --> 00:18:11,780
Not as a crowd.

264
00:18:11,780 --> 00:18:16,280
As a name you have said before, in a house you have already walked through.

265
00:18:16,280 --> 00:18:19,850
Say their names, since no one else will today.

266
00:18:19,850 --> 00:18:25,380
Jesus said that not one sparrow falls to the ground outside the Father's care.

267
00:18:25,380 --> 00:18:28,120
He said the hairs of your head are numbered.

268
00:18:28,120 --> 00:18:35,340
And he said that to people who were about to be handed over, arrested, dragged in front of officials for his name.

269
00:18:35,340 --> 00:18:38,230
He did not say the sparrow never falls.

270
00:18:38,230 --> 00:18:41,090
He said the sparrow never falls unnoticed.

271
00:18:41,090 --> 00:18:44,330
That is a harder comfort and a better one.

272
00:18:44,330 --> 00:18:47,480
He was not promising them a life where nothing breaks.

273
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:53,720
He was telling them that nothing about them was too small to be counted, even in the worst week of their lives.

274
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:56,460
So here is what settles me this morning.

275
00:18:56,460 --> 00:19:02,230
If you are counting sparrows, you are counting the parts of today that no one else will ever notice.

276
00:19:02,230 --> 00:19:06,490
The tiredness behind my eyes that I will not mention to anyone.

277
00:19:06,490 --> 00:19:11,280
The three minutes I will spend in the car before I go inside, gathering myself.

278
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:15,280
The thing I will do well today that nobody will thank me for.

279
00:19:15,280 --> 00:19:18,910
The kind sentence I will say that nobody will repeat.

280
00:19:18,910 --> 00:19:22,140
None of that falls outside your attention.

281
00:19:22,140 --> 00:19:25,600
Earlier I thanked you for the hours I cannot remember.

282
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:28,350
This is the same mercy in daylight.

283
00:19:28,350 --> 00:19:34,070
What you did in the dark while I slept, you are doing in the details while I am awake.

284
00:19:34,070 --> 00:19:37,090
You have never handed me off to anyone.

285
00:19:37,090 --> 00:19:40,480
You have never lost track of a single day I have lived.

286
00:19:40,480 --> 00:19:44,230
You have never once been careless with my life.

287
00:19:44,230 --> 00:19:48,960
So I am deciding something before my feet touch the floor.

288
00:19:48,960 --> 00:19:53,020
I choose to believe that this day already has your footprints on it.

289
00:19:53,020 --> 00:19:58,090
I will not spend this morning rehearsing conversations that may never happen.

290
00:19:58,090 --> 00:20:02,080
I will not treat my own worry as if it were preparation.

291
00:20:02,080 --> 00:20:05,150
I trust you with the hour I am most afraid of.

292
00:20:05,150 --> 00:20:08,220
I trust you with the answer I have not received.

293
00:20:08,220 --> 00:20:12,626
I trust you with the part of today I have not even imagined yet.

294
00:20:12,626 --> 00:20:14,316
And I will move.

295
00:20:14,316 --> 00:20:16,596
I will do the next thing in front of me.

296
00:20:16,596 --> 00:20:25,156
I will make the call, open the message, have the conversation, and take the step, knowing that I am not the one breaking the ground.

297
00:20:25,156 --> 00:20:28,806
And I am going to start with the one I have been avoiding longest.

298
00:20:28,806 --> 00:20:32,766
Not because I feel brave this morning, because I do not.

299
00:20:32,766 --> 00:20:43,016
But because standing still has cost me more than any of these things ever have, and because whatever is on the other side of that door, you are already in the room.

300
00:20:43,016 --> 00:20:47,386
If today goes the way I hope, I will remember who went first.

301
00:20:47,386 --> 00:20:55,936
And if it does not, I will still be walking behind the same God, and I will not go looking for another shelter.

302
00:20:55,936 --> 00:20:59,526
I am not the first one walking into today.

303
00:20:59,526 --> 00:21:02,326
So listen to this before you stand up.

304
00:21:02,326 --> 00:21:06,406
Deuteronomy, chapter thirty-one, verse eight.

305
00:21:06,406 --> 00:21:08,136
He goes before you.

306
00:21:08,136 --> 00:21:09,776
He is with you.

307
00:21:09,776 --> 00:21:13,166
He will not fail you and he will not abandon you.

308
00:21:13,166 --> 00:21:16,826
That was not written for the easy season of a man's life.

309
00:21:16,826 --> 00:21:21,256
It was written for the morning he stepped into something he had never done before.

310
00:21:21,256 --> 00:21:24,586
You woke up tired of a day that had not happened yet.

311
00:21:24,586 --> 00:21:27,076
Someone has already walked into it.

312
00:21:27,076 --> 00:21:28,876
The conversation.

313
00:21:28,876 --> 00:21:30,806
The news you are waiting on.

314
00:21:30,806 --> 00:21:33,016
The person you have to face.

315
00:21:33,016 --> 00:21:35,646
The work still leaning on this morning.

316
00:21:35,646 --> 00:21:38,876
All four have now been prayed over by name.

317
00:21:38,876 --> 00:21:42,496
His going ahead of you never meant the road would be easy.

318
00:21:42,496 --> 00:21:46,836
It means you are not first, and you are not alone.

319
00:21:46,836 --> 00:21:51,816
You can choose that now, standing right here, before you have any proof.

320
00:21:51,816 --> 00:21:54,636
Look down at the road in front of you.

321
00:21:54,636 --> 00:21:57,256
The prints are already there.

322
00:21:57,256 --> 00:22:00,066
You are following, not leading.

323
00:22:00,066 --> 00:22:01,686
Breathe once.

324
00:22:01,686 --> 00:22:04,666
Nothing has to be figured out in the next minute.

325
00:22:04,666 --> 00:22:10,176
May the God who goes before you keep every hour you have not walked into yet.

326
00:22:10,176 --> 00:22:14,066
May he speak your name in the rooms where you are not standing.

327
00:22:14,066 --> 00:22:18,616
May he move what is standing in your road before you reach it.

328
00:22:18,616 --> 00:22:23,946
And if he has not moved it yet, may you know that he is standing right there with you.

329
00:22:23,946 --> 00:22:30,196
Everything you have asked this morning, leave it in hands that were here before you woke up.

330
00:22:30,196 --> 00:22:31,976
In the name of Jesus.

331
00:22:31,976 --> 00:22:33,406
Amen.

332
00:22:33,406 --> 00:22:37,436
If you agree with that, type one word in the comments.

333
00:22:37,436 --> 00:22:38,836
Ahead.

334
00:22:38,836 --> 00:22:40,246
Just that.

335
00:22:40,246 --> 00:22:44,846
Then send this to someone you know is walking into something hard before tonight.

336
00:22:44,846 --> 00:22:48,176
It may be the only prayer said over them today.

337
00:22:48,176 --> 00:22:53,236
And if this is how you want to meet him tomorrow, we will be here at this same hour.

338
00:22:53,236 --> 00:22:56,666
A like helps someone else find this in the dark.

339
00:22:56,666 --> 00:22:59,256
We prayed the hard question this morning.

340
00:22:59,256 --> 00:23:03,206
There is one more, and it does not belong to dawn.

341
00:23:03,206 --> 00:23:09,476
It belongs to the hour when this quiet starts to thin and the day asks you to prove you meant it.

342
00:23:09,476 --> 00:23:13,066
That prayer is waiting for you right here.
